{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CnqbGjiENpv2aZYXbaqCyY","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /tmp/h-aPUe9E/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cf36742-a3f5-449e-af65-0e89f003cad8","uuid":"90f68585-ddf8-4daf-81d9-a505b1641b49","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:04:27.703Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/tmp/h-aPUe9E/README.md","oldString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Prompt caching is on: the static\ncoaching instructions are their own system block with a `cache_control` marker, and\nthe per-athlete block (facts, date) follows it uncached, so a `save_fact` does not\nevict the instructions from cache.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":7,"lines":[" Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type"," messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).","-Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the static","+coaching instructions are their own system block with a `cache_control` marker, and","+the per-athlete block (facts, date) follows it uncached, so a `save_fact` does not","+evict the instructions from cache."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CnqbGjiENpv2aZYXbaqCyY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzyomEsD5UwNNKiFRJD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ScMbMupq1bZCxUD1VwKvnK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/h-aPUe9E/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix: save_fact evicts the cached system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete context\n(including the long-term facts list and today's date) into one system block, and\nput the `cache_control` marker on that whole block. The cache is keyed on the exact\nprefix up to the marker, so any change to the facts list invalidated the whole\ncached prefix. `save_fact` appends to that list, so the next call wrote the cache\nagain (`cache_creation_input_tokens` ~1000) and read nothing (`cache_read_input_tokens: 0`).\nThat is the pattern in `logs/usage.jsonl` and `NOTES.md`. The date changing each day\nhad the same effect.\n\n## Change\n\n`bot.py`, `build_system()`: the system prompt is now two blocks.\n\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, static, with `cache_control: ephemeral`.\n2. `athlete_context(...)` (name, zones, goal, facts, date, language), no cache marker.\n\nA `save_fact` now changes only block 2, which sits after the breakpoint, so block 1\nstill hits the cache. Rule 16 (\"do not save a fact already in the list below\") still\nholds, because block 2 is still in the same system prompt after the instructions.\n\n`README.md`: the caching paragraph now describes the split.\n\nNo change to tool selection (`select_tools`), per the NOTES.md decision.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Checked in memory without calling the API or writing to `logs/usage.jsonl` or\n  `data/athletes.json`: the cached block (block 1) is identical before and after a\n  `save_fact` and a date change; the athlete block changes; the marker is only on block 1.\n- Not verified against the real API. There is no `anthropic` SDK or\n  `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY` in this environment, and I did not make API calls.\n\n## Open risk: the cached prefix may be under the minimum size\n\nCaching only happens if the prefix up to the marker is at least 1024 tokens on\nSonnet models. The prefix is tool definitions plus block 1. Block 1 is about\n2,500 characters, and the core tools are about 400 characters more. My rough\nestimate is around 700 to 1000 tokens, and the logged first cache writes (~1,046\ntokens with the facts block included) suggest the static part is close to or\njust under 1024. If it is under, the breakpoint is ignored and this change would\nturn caching off for every call, not just after `save_fact`.\n\nTo check after deploy, look at the next few `usage.jsonl` lines:\n\n- A first call should show `cache_creation_input_tokens` ~ the static size, and the\n  next call in the window should show `cache_read_input_tokens` ~ the same and\n  `cache_creation_input_tokens` near 0.\n- After a `save_fact`, the next call should still show `cache_read_input_tokens` > 0.\n- If `cache_creation_input_tokens` and `cache_read_input_tokens` are both 0 on the\n  static part, the prefix is below the minimum. The fix there is to make the static\n  prefix longer with useful content, not to pad it.\n\n## Other notes\n\n- Keyword tool selection changes the tool list, which is part of the prefix, so\n  messages that add a group (e.g. `plan_week`) still miss the cache. That was already\n  true and was judged worth it in March; this change does not affect it.\n- Nothing was deployed, published or reported to any external service.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":36106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session